WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.700
Configuration management supports cybersecurity by reducing unnecessary variability and helping teams maintain secure settings.

2
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:13.240
Consistent configurations are easier to protect, monitor, and troubleshoot.

3
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:22.800
Good configuration management supports vulnerability management because teams can identify installed software, patch levels, and affected systems more reliably.

4
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.120
It also improves incident response and detection.

5
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:33.180
When defenders know what normal configurations should look like, unexpected changes become easier to identify and investigate.

6
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:39.220
Many security problems become worse when configurations are unknown or unmanaged.

7
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:46.920
Configuration management strengthens defensive visibility and control by making system states more predictable and accountable.
